# A project's own values for init-env.sh, read on every start over the
# template's defaults. Copy this file to project.env, in this folder, set the
# lines your project needs and commit it. The template ships no project.env, so
# init-env.sh stays identical to the template's; keep this file identical too,
# so that a value the template adds shows in template-sync.sh as drift.
#
# NAME=VALUE lines, # comments and blank lines. A name init-env.sh does not
# know stops the start.

# The exact Frappe release install-bench.sh installs, the one your production
# image is built from, and the Python and Node frappe/build carries at that
# tag. Written into .env when it is created; an existing .env keeps its own.
#DEFAULT_FRAPPE_VERSION=v16.35.0
#DEFAULT_FRAPPE_PYTHON=3.14.7
#DEFAULT_FRAPPE_NODE=24.21.0

# The internal domains the containers reach without the proxy, comma-separated.
# Written into .env on every start.
#NO_PROXY_DOMAINS=.example.org,git.example.org
